186045417] [17592186135454 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135454 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186429841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135454 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ed2b163e-f418-5803-9223-687190c52195" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138135 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13752" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138135 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $4$ raised to the second power." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138135 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b5313725-78fc-57ee-9acc-19d03f6624bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138135 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to evaluate $4^2.$\n\nTo evaluate $4^2,$ we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{2}={{4\\times 4}_{⏟}}_{\\text{[math]2[/math] times}}=16\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138136 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13754" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138136 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $5$ raised to the power of $3?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138136 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "213a088d-3427-5313-adc2-1fcc9d64bb74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138136 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, $5$ raised to the power of $3$ means $5^3.$\n\nTo compute this power, we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n![](images/e7/e7beecad2379c3be9452eb111496ed8c65a5d4f747874658167169bba6ff11c9.svg)\n\nNow, we compute the product. Since $5 \\times 5 = 25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{5\\times 5}_{⏟}}_{25}\\times 5 & =25\\times 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out ${\\color{blue}25} \\times 5.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{}_{2}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5^3=125.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138137 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13757" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138137 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $6^1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138137 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c0e05b6-e633-5b9e-a070-3e26e0349355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138137 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, ${\\color{blue}6}^{\\color{red}1}$ is in exponent form. The base is $\\color{blue}6$ and the exponent is ${\\color{red}1}.$ \n\nThis means that $\\color{blue}6$ is taken as a factor only once. Therefore,\n\n$$\n6^1 = 6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138138 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13760" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138138 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the value of $0^5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138138 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d4e63087-a01f-59b3-bf6c-cf7cbfa3ce78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138138 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, ${\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{red}5}$ is in exponent form. The base is $\\color{blue}0$ and the exponent is ${\\color{red}5}.$ \n\nThis means that ${\\color{blue}0}$ is taken as a factor ${\\color{red}5}$ times. Therefore,\n![](images/ac/acfc8529f86ae7a3d9082c541da994c0c69ffccf33d01226593ae61cfb4d263a.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186138712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186138861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1039 "Squaring a Number" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186138135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138401 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9c336cc3-c89e-5af2-b170-1fc6d9cf8307" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138402 #edb/ref 1037 #e